<title>CHILE: Chile bank earnings up 32 pct Jan-June vs year ago.</title>
<headline>Chile bank earnings up 32 pct Jan-June vs year ago.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's banking and financial sector reported net earnings of 154 billion pesos in the six months to June, up 32 percent from the same period last year, the Banks and Financial Institutions Superintendency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The figures showed loan portfolios grew 11.7 percent against the first six months of 1996, with consumer credits climbing 29 percent. Trade loans rose 12.6 percent, while foreign credits were down 13 percent.</p>
<p>The following is a list showing net earnings of some individual banks in the six months to June.</p>
<p>				June 1997		June 1996</p>
<p>Banco BHIF		    6.36		    6.00</p>
<p>Banco de A. Edwards	12.00		    9.51</p>
<p>Banco de Chile	     34.19		   11.75*</p>
<p>Banco de Credito e Inv   12.24		   11.25</p>
<p>Banco Santiago	     33.48		    n/a</p>
<p>Banco Santander-Chile    12.47		   10.69</p>
<p>NOTES: * These 1996 figures are after repayment of subordinated debt to the central bank.</p>
<p>All figures are in billions of pesos. The 1996 figures are in peso terms from that year and are not expressed in 1997 pesos.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
